  - line: 17
    type: scene_header
    text: "---"
  - line: 18
    type: narration
    text: "scene 026.1 — the sound of water"
  - line: 20
    type: narration
    text: "scene meta:"
  - line: 21
    type: narration
    text: "location: Compound Tunnels / Subterranean Caverns"
  - line: 22
    type: narration
    text: "time: year 17,503 (Three weeks after scene 025.5)"
  - line: 23
    type: narration
    text: "participants: The Nameless One (Geralt), Applicator (internal)"
  - line: 24
    type: narration
    text: "focus: Three weeks after the uprising, Geralt recovers and explores deep subterranean tunnels guided by the sound of trickling water, discovering a portal-like pond that exists adjacent to normal reality."
  - line: 25
    type: narration
    text: "continuity: Three weeks after scene 025.5"
  - line: 26
    type: narration
    text: "presentation: cutscene"
  - line: 27
    type: narration
    text: "cutscene purpose: Establish Geralt's physical recovery, his desire for true spoken language, and his discovery of the subterranean portal pond."
  - line: 29
    type: narration
    text: "The Sound of Water"
  - line: 31
    type: narration
    text: "Strength returned to The Nameless One in increments measured by pain's recession."
  - line: 32
    type: narration
    text: "Each day brought fractional improvement—ribs that ground with every breath began to merely ache."
  - line: 33
    type: narration
    text: "Spine that had shattered found ways to knit itself together through processes that should have been impossible."
  - line: 34
    type: narration
    text: "The Applicator's presence remained mostly dormant during recovery, offering only the minimal support necessary to keep catastrophic damage from becoming fatal."
  - line: 36
    type: narration
    text: "Conserving resources, it had explained during one brief moment of communication."
  - line: 37
    type: narration
    text: "Both of us need time to heal."
  - line: 38
    type: narration
    text: "Rest, host."
  - line: 39
    type: narration
    text: "I'll wake when necessary."
  - line: 41
    type: narration
    text: "The compound transformed around him as he recovered."
  - line: 42
    type: narration
    text: "What had been prison became something approaching home—not through nostalgia or comfort, but through choice."
  - line: 43
    type: narration
    text: "The freed slaves had decided to claim this place rather than flee from it, to make it represent their will rather than abandon it to memory of suffering."
  - line: 45
    type: narration
    text: "The dormitories were rebuilt as individual dwellings."
  - line: 46
    type: narration
    text: "The mining equipment was repurposed for construction."
  - line: 47
    type: narration
    text: "Gardens were planted in spaces that had known only stone and despair."
  - line: 48
    type: narration
    text: "Children—the few that existed—played in areas where screams had once echoed."
  - line: 50
    type: narration
    text: "And everywhere, the sophisticated gesture-language they'd developed allowed communication that approached true complexity."
  - line: 51
    type: narration
    text: "Not speech, but close enough that communities could organize, could debate, could dream together about futures that extended beyond simple survival."
  - line: 53
    type: narration
    text: "But The Nameless One felt the limitation acutely."
  - line: 54
    type: narration
    text: "Gestures were remarkable tools—far superior to the grunts and crude signals they'd started with—but they remained tools."
  - line: 55
    type: narration
    text: "Inadequate for poetry."
  - line: 56
    type: narration
    text: "Insufficient for philosophy."
  - line: 57
    type: narration
    text: "Unable to capture the full complexity of thought that churned through consciousness recovering from trauma and invasion and revelation."
  - line: 59
    type: narration
    text: "He wanted to speak."
  - line: 61
    type: narration
    text: "To form words with tongue and teeth and breath."
  - line: 62
    type: narration
    text: "To give sound to ideas that gesture-language could only approximate."
  - line: 63
    type: narration
    text: "To say things that hands simply couldn't express."
  - line: 65
    type: narration
    text: "The desire grew stronger each day."
  - line: 66
    type: narration
    text: "An ache that had nothing to do with healing bones and everything to do with consciousness that had tasted power—the power of stopping whips, of organizing resistance, of negotiating with parasitic invader—and found it wanted more."
  - line: 68
    type: narration
    text: "Wanted the power of language itself."
  - line: 70
    type: scene_header
    text: "---"
  - line: 72
    type: narration
    text: "Three weeks after the battle, strong enough to walk without assistance, The Nameless One began exploring the compound's deeper sections."
  - line: 73
    type: narration
    text: "Areas that had been off-limits during slavery, sealed by Anunnaki authority, forbidden on pain of immediate execution."
  - line: 75
    type: narration
    text: "But no masters remained to forbid."
  - line: 76
    type: narration
    text: "No Overseers to punish."
  - line: 77
    type: narration
    text: "Just empty passages waiting to reveal whatever secrets they'd hidden."
  - line: 79
    type: narration
    text: "The scarred one had offered to accompany him, concern evident in her gestures, but he'd declined with appreciation that transcended their limited communication."
  - line: 80
    type: narration
    text: "This felt like something he needed to do alone."
  - line: 81
    type: narration
    text: "A pull that came from somewhere beyond conscious decision—instinct or perhaps something deeper, something that had been calling since the crystalline chamber's visions, since the Applicator's revelations about networks and purposes and ancient machinations."
  - line: 83
    type: narration
    text: "He descended through levels that showed geological layers like pages in history book."
  - line: 84
    type: narration
    text: "Stone that dated from the compound's construction gave way to formations older than human civilization, then to rock that predated the Anunnaki's arrival entirely."
  - line: 85
    type: narration
    text: "The air grew cooler as he went deeper, carrying mineral scents that spoke of water and time and patience measured in eons."
  - line: 87
    type: narration
    text: "And then—sound."
  - line: 89
    type: narration
    text: "Faint."
  - line: 90
    type: narration
    text: "Rhythmic."
  - line: 91
    type: narration
    text: "The trickle of water moving through stone."
  - line: 93
    type: narration
    text: "The Nameless One paused, head tilted, listening with intensity that transcended normal hearing."
  - line: 94
    type: narration
    text: "Not just water."
  - line: 95
    type: narration
    text: "Something more."
  - line: 96
    type: narration
    text: "A quality to the sound that suggested... invitation?"
  - line: 97
    type: narration
    text: "Recognition?"
  - line: 98
    type: narration
    text: "The sense that whatever produced that trickling had been waiting specifically for someone to hear it, to follow it, to discover what lay at its source."
  - line: 100
    type: narration
    text: "Host, the Applicator stirred from dormancy with unusual sharpness."
  - line: 101
    type: narration
    text: "I recognize that sound frequency."
  - line: 102
    type: narration
    text: "Those are not natural acoustics."
  - line: 104
    type: narration
    text: "What do you mean?"
  - line: 106
    type: narration
    text: "The water."
  - line: 107
    type: narration
    text: "It's flowing through crystalline formations similar to those in the chamber we built."
  - line: 108
    type: narration
    text: "This is deliberate."
  - line: 109
    type: narration
    text: "Constructed."
  - line: 110
    type: narration
    text: "Someone—something—created this."
  - line: 112
    type: narration
    text: "The Nameless One felt his pulse quicken."
  - line: 113
    type: narration
    text: "The Nephoretti?"
  - line: 115
    type: narration
    text: "Unknown."
  - line: 116
    type: narration
    text: "But probable."
  - line: 117
    type: narration
    text: "The frequency signature matches what I've cataloged as pre-Anunnaki technology."
  - line: 118
    type: narration
    text: "Whatever created this system predates our makers."
  - line: 120
    type: narration
    text: "Should we—"
  - line: 122
    type: narration
    text: "Continue, the Applicator's tone carried unusual emphasis."
  - line: 123
    type: narration
    text: "This may be exactly what you've been seeking."
  - line: 124
    type: narration
    text: "The gifts you need."
  - line: 125
    type: narration
    text: "The transformation required for what comes next."
  - line: 127
    type: narration
    text: "The Nameless One followed the sound through passages that narrowed until he moved sideways, until stone pressed against his chest and back simultaneously, until claustrophobia threatened to overwhelm determination."
  - line: 129
    type: narration
    text: "Then the passage opened."
  - line: 131
    type: narration
    text: "Into a chamber that stole breath and replaced it with wonder."
  - line: 133
    type: scene_header
    text: "---"
  - line: 135
    type: narration
    text: "The space was vast—impossibly vast given that it existed deep beneath the compound's foundations, carved from living stone in ways that suggested natural formation and deliberate architecture simultaneously."
  - line: 136
    type: narration
    text: "Bioluminescent growths covered the walls like stars scattered across night sky, providing light that was just sufficient to see but insufficient to banish mystery."
  - line: 138
    type: narration
    text: "And in the chamber's center—a pond."
  - line: 140
    type: narration
    text: "Not large."
  - line: 141
    type: narration
    text: "Perhaps twenty feet across."
  - line: 142
    type: narration
    text: "But deep—the Nameless One could see the bottom dropping away into darkness that suggested the water descended far beyond sight, connecting to aquifers or underground rivers or spaces that existed beyond conventional mapping."
  - line: 144
    type: narration
    text: "The surface was perfectly still despite the trickling sound that had led him here."
  - line: 145
    type: narration
    text: "Glass-smooth."
  - line: 146
    type: narration
    text: "Reflecting the bioluminescent lights with mirror precision that made it difficult to determine where water ended and reflection began."
  - line: 148
    type: narration
    text: "Beautiful."
  - line: 149
    type: narration
    text: "Serene."
  - line: 150
    type: narration
    text: "And utterly, impossibly wrong."
  - line: 152
    type: narration
    text: "Host, the Applicator's presence consolidated with sharp attention."
  - line: 153
    type: narration
    text: "The water."
  - line: 154
    type: narration
    text: "It's not behaving according to physical laws."
  - line: 155
    type: narration
    text: "Surface tension is... negotiable here."
  - line: 156
    type: narration
    text: "This space exists adjacent to normal reality."
  - line: 158
    type: narration
    text: "What does that mean?"
  - line: 160
    type: narration
    text: "It means we're standing at threshold."
  - line: 161
    type: narration
    text: "Boundary between physical realm and something else."
  - line: 162
    type: narration
    text: "The Ethereal Realm, perhaps."
  - line: 163
    type: narration
    text: "Or spaces that don't have names in your limited vocabulary."
  - line: 165
    type: narration
    text: "The Nameless One approached the pond's edge slowly, every sense screaming contradictory warnings—danger and safety, threat and invitation, fear and desperate hope all tangled together until they became indistinguishable."
  - line: 167
    type: narration
    text: "He knelt at the water's edge."
  - line: 168
    type: narration
    text: "Extended his hand."
  - line: 169
    type: narration
    text: "Touched surface that felt like water but somehow... more."
  - line: 170
    type: narration
    text: "Denser."
  - line: 171
    type: narration
    text: "More aware."
  - line: 172
    type: narration
    text: "As though the pond itself possessed consciousness, possessed purpose, possessed patience that had waited through ages for this specific moment."
  - line: 174
    type: narration
    text: "The water rippled at his touch despite there being no physical disturbance to create ripples."
  - line: 175
    type: narration
    text: "Waves spread outward in perfect circles, growing larger, intensifying, until the entire pond's surface churned with motion that had no physical source."
  - line: 177
    type: narration
    text: "And from the depths—they rose."
  - line: 179
    type: scene_header
    text: "---"
  - line: 181
    type: narration
    text: "~Year 17,503 (Immediately following scene 026.1)"

